#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet: start, stop and manage the multi-device monitoring stack with one command.

  ./fleet up                  start everything and wait until it is ready
  ./fleet down [--wipe]       stop everything (asks first, confirms afterwards)
  ./fleet status              stack health and a device summary
  ./fleet list [--json]       every device: state, last seen, readings
  ./fleet check <id>          one device in detail
  ./fleet add <id>            onboard a device: shows what to run on it, waits for it to appear
  ./fleet remove <id>         forget a retired device (deletes its stored data, asks first)
  ./fleet notify set|test|status|off   send alerts to Discord, Slack, Telegram or a webhook

Run it on the machine that hosts the stack. Needs Docker with Compose v2 and Python 3.9+, nothing else.
Demonstration tool: no authentication or TLS anywhere (see README, Known limitations).
"""
